akhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0ac8d4026cdde624d1633314b7b2cb3e25dcf1001e3aec17afd92e2142e1ac4b","event_uuid":"36aa6625-6cff-46bc-8f3a-1bec22c1a7c7","position":{"commit_sha":"1c7ea90452c4aab51bc342208ff9cc21f75bc3b0","position":"1786825242491948001-36aa6625-6cff-46bc-8f3a-1bec22c1a7c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f4434260bfc18fe5e9043a9ba872e5105e99f3f0346eed130bce62c111f6321e","event_uuid":"24b9e042-2046-4837-aa95-1f7e0bf92f05","position":{"commit_sha":"188dd6851ea96cfb2fbf97549f53b1b16e4d6157","position":"1786825370080425001-24b9e042-2046-4837-aa95-1f7e0bf92f05"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"32d240b3ec4cc5b013c81afea50f560fae46283e039c3bdbf83cbdaf585dc011","event_uuid":"1e18da86-921f-4b31-a40d-b59ffca3dacd","position":{"commit_sha":"78a0dda60056788503233f0b8f85b9fb68bea7df","position":"1786825993206050001-1e18da86-921f-4b31-a40d-b59ffca3dacd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fef5d135f2bc9ca15ed7d6ac5c6989d304476c8df287900e0d4943f06d3a502c","event_uuid":"1e019a54-c606-43c0-9ebb-3bc4216c06de","position":{"commit_sha":"bb26e4e3f28829c0947d6ab06a4894d99b15a87b","position":"1786826001299856001-1e019a54-c606-43c0-9ebb-3bc4216c06de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786808978813161001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cb9b437c-4237-45e7-9786-7bf43a842f5b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a011-491c-f7e5-4dd9"},{"link_uuid":"e54c9615-4477-40d2-9846-c73ad6105b06","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27"},{"link_uuid":"ab8dba49-9a9c-4391-9fa0-114da95f0577","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"da0c-efa6-4c11-44a0"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThe bridge project mapping (`.bridge_state/projects.json` — mapped keys + `legacy_default`)\ncan hold syntactically-valid-but-nonexistent or bot-invisible Jira project keys. Ticket F adds\nSYNTACTIC write-time validation only (deliberately: a live call in the `set_project` write path\ncouples a local config write to Jira availability/auth, adds latency/flakiness, blocks legitimate\nbootstrapping/provisioning order, and is TOCTOU-insufficient anyway). Ticket D adds an at-pass-time\nEXISTENCE/visibility preflight inside the reconcile pass (the authoritative mutation guard).\n\nNeither gives an operator an on-demand, non-blocking way to ask \"are my mapped keys + legacy_default\nactually visible to the bot right now?\" outside a full reconcile pass. The projects.json corruption\nincident (bug 05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27) would have been caught immediately by such a diagnostic.\n\n## Scope (approved: additive diagnostic on the BRIDGE surface only)\n\nAdd an OPT-IN, credential-conditional, READ-ONLY, ADVISORY live mapped-key/legacy_default visibility\ncheck to the existing `rebar bridge fsck` verb, gated behind a new `--live-visibility` flag.\n\nHard constraints (separation of concerns — Jira stays an optional extra):\n1. Live check lives ONLY on the bridge surface. Do NOT add it to core `rebar doctor`\n   (`src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`) — that command is store/tracker health and MUST stay Jira-free\n   (no reconciler / `[agents]` optional-extra import from core doctor).\n2. Do NOT introduce a `bridge doctor` verb (epic 2f79 deliberately declined it — reuse `bridge fsck`).\n3. Reuse D's mapped-project visibility helper — ONE shared helper answers \"are the mapped keys +\n   legacy_default visible to the bot?\". Do NOT hand-roll a second Jira existence check (that is the\n   duplicated-existence-check parity smell this epic has been eliminating). This is why G depends_on D.\n   The shared helper is `rebar_reconciler.access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility(repo_root, *,\n   probe=None, client_cls, env=None, query_project=None, projects_store_mod=None) ->\n   ProjectVisibilityResult(status, required, visible, missing, detail)` where status is one of\n   {ok, missing, transport_unavailable, skipped}.\n4. Credential-conditional graceful degradation: the NEW fsck-layer step performs its OWN\n   `JIRA_URL`/`JIRA_USER`/`JIRA_API_TOKEN` presence check FIRST (mirroring `run_access_check`'s\n   `missing_credentials` contract in `access_check.py`) and, when any is absent/incomplete AND no\n   `probe=` is injected, emits an advisory `skipped` verdict with `reason=\"missing_credentials\"`\n   WITHOUT calling the probe. Only when creds are present (or a `probe=` is injected for tests) does\n   the step call `check_mapped_project_visibility(probe=...)`. This is the fsck layer bridging the\n   helper's own `transport_unavailable`-on-absent-creds behavior into the operator-facing\n   \"skipped — no live credentials\" advisory. The step MUST skip cleanly, NOT fail.\n5. Read-only + advisory: no Jira writes; no bridge-state mutation; the new step reports drift but does\n   NOT change `bridge fsck`'s existing pass/fail exit contract.\n\n## Surfacing the verdict (data flow when `--live-visibility` IS passed)\n\nTo keep the pinned `bridge_fsck.schema.json` output contract UNCHANGED (its `required` set and the\n`test_bridge_fsck_schema_pins_new_required_fields_and_integrity_kinds` contract test both fix the\ntop-level JSON to exactly `{unknown_event_types, binding_drift, store_integrity}` under\n`additionalProperties: false`), the `--live-visibility` advisory is rendered as human-readable lines\nto STDERR (a separate stream) in BOTH text and `--output json` modes. It is NOT added as a new field\nto the stdout JSON findings object, so no schema or schema-contract-test change is required and the\ndefault (no-flag) stdout is byte-identical to today. The step's structured verdict dict is returned by\na directly-unit-testable helper (`audit_mapped_project_visibility(...)`) which main() renders to stderr.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge fsck --live-visibility` gains a mapped-project live-visibility step that, WHEN live\n  creds are present, lists each mapped key + legacy_default and reports visible / NOT-visible-to-bot\n  by calling the shared helper `access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility`; the advisory is written\n  to stderr and does not alter the exit code.\n- [x] WHEN live creds (`JIRA_URL`/`JIRA_USER`/`JIRA_API_TOKEN`) are absent/incomplete AND no `probe=` is\n  injected, the fsck-layer step's own presence check emits an advisory verdict\n  `{\"status\":\"skipped\",\"reason\":\"missing_credentials\"}` WITHOUT calling the probe, and `bridge fsck`\n  behaves exactly as today (no crash, exit contract unchanged).\n- [x] The visibility logic is the SAME helper D uses (`check_mapped_project_visibility`, injected via the\n  `probe=` seam) — no duplicate existence check; verified by test.\n- [x] Core `rebar doctor` imports remain Jira-free (no new reconciler/`[agents]` import reachable from\n  `_commands/doctor.py`); verified by test.\n- [x] The default `rebar bridge fsck` (no `--live-visibility`) stdout JSON contract is unchanged (exactly\n  `unknown_event_types`, `binding_drift`, `store_integrity`); `bridge_fsck.schema.json` and its contract\n  test are untouched.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN always-on unit tests in `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py`, run with\n`python -m pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py -q`:\n- (a) creds-present path with a `probe=` injected showing a mapped key invisible → the step's verdict is\n  `status=\"missing\"` and names the invisible key.\n- (b) creds-absent path (no probe, empty/partial `JIRA_*` env) → the step's own presence check returns\n  `status=\"skipped\"`, `reason=\"missing_credentials\"`, no probe call, no hard failure, exit contract\n  unchanged.\n- (c) all-visible `probe=` → `status=\"ok\"`.\n- (d) core-`rebar doctor`-stays-Jira-free assertion (no reconciler import reachable from\n  `_commands/doctor.py`).\nAlso `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; no real network calls in tests (patch the `probe=` seam).\n\n## Notes\n- Depends on D for the shared visibility helper (`access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility`).\n- Same workflow as A/B/D: fresh worktree off origin/main, review-plan → sign-review → claim, RED→GREEN\n  TDD, make lint/typecheck + targeted pytest, commit -s with rebar-ticket trailer, push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_visibility.py","reason":"New sibling module: opt-in credential-conditional live mapped-key visibility diagnostic reusing D's shared access_check.check_mapped_project_visibility helper; lazy access_check loader and advisory formatter"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"Add --live-visibility flag and wire the advisory into main, rendered to stderr; stdout JSON contract and exit code unchanged"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"Document --live-visibility in the bridge fsck help text"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py","reason":"RED to GREEN unit tests: probe-injected missing/ok, creds-absent skip, --live-visibility stderr advisory keeps 3-key JSON, core doctor stays Jira-free"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a011-491c-f7e5-4dd9"],["relates_to","da0c-efa6-4c11-44a0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1e18da86-921f-4b31-a40d-b59ffca3dacd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9702-12c7-fd3a-47c1","ticket_type":"story","title":"bridge fsck: opt-in live mapped-key visibility diagnostic","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["59c2b506-bd07-4794-b5d7-e098f394a65d","d2bf9051-9658-44ec-a982-cd77d158e3fd","1bdbdf1c-47db-4ca3-8a20-edf9b9546bed","192f51ea-93c9-4679-adf9-4ed851af8aed","d986584a-93b6-4ebd-8928-64c2ba93815c","7d076836-fa14-48c9-8f2e-dd6f8eb1f741","ab8dba49-9a9c-4391-9fa0-114da95f0577","e4f200be-8a3d-40ac-a1ea-afaf1f223270","36aa6625-6cff-46bc-8f3a-1bec22c1a7c7","24b9e042-2046-4837-aa95-1f7e0bf92f05","1e18da86-921f-4b31-a40d-b59ffca3dacd","1e019a54-c606-43c0-9ebb-3bc4216c06de"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786828302458730001,"uuid":"9630bc7a-63ae-4f68-8441-12e7c2ef9dcc"}